<article class="env-lemma" id="0CY6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CY6">Lemma <span data-tag="0CY6">10.31.7</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a ring map. Let $R \to R'$ be of finite type. If $S$ is Noetherian, then the base change $S' = R' \otimes _ R S$ is Noetherian. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/05G5" data-tag="05G5">10.14.2</a> finite type is stable under base change. Thus $S \to S'$ is of finite type. Since $S$ is Noetherian we can apply Lemma <a href="/tag/00FN" data-tag="00FN">10.31.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>